<title>NETHERLANDS: KLM orders four Boeing 737s.</title>
<headline>KLM orders four Boeing 737s.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-03-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>KLM Royal Dutch Airlines said on Friday it had placed an order for four Boeing 737-800 short and medium range aircraft.</p>
<p>The Dutch carrier said the twin-engined aircraft will be equipped with CFM56-7 engines and the purchase price would be around $190 million.  </p>
<p>KLM said the planes would strengthen its European fleet into the 21st century and are expected to be delivered in the summer of 1999. The company said it would use the planes in a 147-seat configuration.</p>
<p>Aircraft engine maker CFM International is a joint venture of France's SNECMA and GE of the United States.</p>
